{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery","id":1129472,"title":"Using Lunar Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-15T16:16:50-07:00","id":1129472,"title":"Using Lunar Sorcery","content":"So, for 1,500 years, the Lunar Exalted were the premier sorcerers in Creation (the Sidereal Exalted are more the premier sorcerers of Yu-Shan who occasionally visited Creation for work). Because they can use Celestial Circle Sorcery, they can potentially create Ambition 3 Solar Workings. If we assume that 20% of the Lunar have Celestial Circle Sorcery, that would mean that there are around 60-80 sorcerers on Creation capable of doing an Ambition 3 Solar Working. If we further assume that 10% of them make one Ambition 3 Solar Working every century, that would mean that Lunar Exalted would have produced 90-120 Ambition 3 Solar Circle Workings, which means that they could have reshaped a fair amount of Creation. What Ambition 3 Solar Workings do you think that the Lunar Exalted have accomplished over the last 1,500 years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:57:58-07:00","id":1129669,"title":"","content":"Them's some broad assumptions on the number of Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> That said, in the lead up to the release, Holden and Morke teased that a neat thing about the Caul was that the Lunars cut it away from the Loom of Fate. I'd buy THAT as being possible with an Ambition 3 Solar Working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":".  Fixing the Autocorrect 08-16-2017, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T07:21:02-07:00","id":1129772,"title":"","content":"Yeah, removing a continent from the Loom (very useful when battling Sidereals) is pretty damn significant.<br /> <br /> Other ideas:<br /> Creating a huge magical oasis teeming with life in the middle of the desert, protected by massive enchanted walls that make it invisible, to create a hidden kingdom for the Lunar's subjects, from which they can strike at the Realm.<br /> Create a flying island full of monsters that can be used as a mobile battlestation.<br /> Create a huge Wyld zone all the way around a country, stopping the Realm daring to attack it.<br /> Enchant a land so that those who eat its food while pregnant give birth to beastmen of the Lunar's totem (what, you think Lunar's give birth to all those beastmen by themselves?)<br /> Create an army of golems inhabited by the souls of the dead of the Lunar's tribe.<br /> Curse a Satrapy so that all children born there are hideous mutants.<br /> Curse a Satrapy so that it becomes a massive wyld zone.<br /> Bless (or curse) the Lunar's subjects so that when they die, their souls possess large animals (lions, horses, elephants, etc).<br /> Bless (or curse) the Lunar's subjects so that when they die, they transform into elementals of the local elements.<br /> Change time at the summit of a mountain so that students who go there can do awesome training montages under the Lunar's tutelage, and become (still mortal) kung-fu masters in a few days.<br /> Create a massive fortress which can think for itself, shoot ballista, use statues to defend itself, and move walls to confuse attackers (you don't live there, you just make the Realm think you do so they waste time trying to invade it).<br /> Bless the entire country's land so that one farmer can produce enough food for 100 people, allowing the people to move into other jobs and spark a massive economic boom.<br /> Create rings of stone that, when someone walks into them, lets them travel along a mysterious fog-shrouded, eerie path, leading to another stone circle, allowing someone to cross a kingdom in an hour. Multiple rings allow the inhabitants to travel all over the country, allowing troops and trade to move wherever they're needed incredibly quickly.<br /> Create a horde of terrifying flying monsters for your armies to ride.<br /> Turn thousands of people into were-wolves (or were-horses, or were-owls, or whatever).<br /> Enchant a land with a strange fog that drives the Lunar's enemies mad, but leaves her subjects and friends untouched.<br /> Mess with dragon lines, so that Satrapy's manses stop working (or blow up), while creating new demesnes far away in the wilderness.<br /> Create a radiation-breathing, super-strong, super-tough, super-stealthy, amphibious Kaiju, who really hates Immaculate temples, and who who lurks in the Inner Sea and periodically appears to destroy cities with Immaculate temples in.<br /> <br /> I think the main thing PCs are going to encounter, in terms of Solar workings made by Lunars, is magically enchanted forests/mountains/countries, or giant ravenous monsters created to attack the Realm (or whoever).<br /> And things to hide them from Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-16-2017, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T07:24:02-07:00","id":1129773,"title":"","content":"Maybe a long term plan to reinforce broad swathes of Creation's borders against the Wyld? If you can't use Wyld Shaping Technique sorcery provides a pretty decent work-around to do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:34:22-07:00","id":1129832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1129772#post1129772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Create a radiation-breathing, super-strong, super-tough, super-stealthy, amphibious Kaiju, who really hates Immaculate temples, and who who lurks in the Inner Sea and periodically appears to destroy cities with Immaculate temples in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be yoinking all of those for future campaigns, but this was a the masterstroke. Actual LOLs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:20:19-07:00","id":1129859,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> I've got to thank Aya Tari for his latest bevy of threads, it's giving me lots of good idea to consider.<br /> I never really thought much about Lunars and the ancient workings they may have made.<br /> If I ever run Exalted again (which I might in a year or two), I'd be tempted to have some countries that were once ruled by an ancient Lunar who created loads of workings.<br /> <br /> It also tempts me to bring back my retired Lunar celestial sorcerer, but the game I play that in has very little downtime, and doing Solar workings requires months of downtime, so it's not much good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:00:23-07:00","id":1129939,"title":"","content":"As a note, assuming Lunars keep their dice adder from the core book, they can hit solar level dicepools. Assuming a maxed out Sorcerer, the math works out to a Finesse 3 Solar 3 Working taking about two years to accomplish. <br /> <br /> A Lunar who managed to get 17 Means (which is basically impossible) could theoretically achieve a Finesse 1 Solar 3 Working with just Int 3, Wits 3, Occult 3 and a good level one stunt on each roll, but it would take 85 years to perform (and probably another couple of decades to gather the supplies, so call it a century).<br /> <br /> So, those should be the two ends of the spectrum as far as time required goes and it should be noted that it's very, very difficult for a Celestial Sorcerer to pull off a Finesse 5 Solar 3 Working, which means that most of these things are not going to be exactly as desired by their creator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:09:50-07:00","id":1129942,"title":"","content":"That just makes them more interesting, from an ST perspective!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:11:11-07:00","id":1129943,"title":"","content":"Though, hmmm.... If a maxxed out Celestial Circle Sorcerer can pull off the highest rank of Workings in as little as two years.... I think that Raksi should probably be assumed to have some method of casting Solar Circle spells by now. Assuming she's still obsessed about that anyway. Said method should also have some side effects however, as she likely had to cut a few corners here and there.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on how she might have done it or what the side effects are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:16:45-07:00","id":1129948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1129942#post1129942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just makes them more interesting, from an ST perspective!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh certainly. I don't necessarily advocate for game rules being equal to phyiscs or anything, but, with Workings we really don't have anything else to extrapolate from and I was getting a bit worried that some people might run off with the idea that Celestial Sorcerers could just crank these out so I wanted to see what the bare minimum times were for putting these sorts of things together and help everyone get a better sense of just how many of them were likely to have been produced.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, the fact that they usually would have to go for Finesse 3 or even 1, is a very fun bit for the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:19:08-07:00","id":1129949,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't put powerful workings past the reach of the Lunar Pact, but keep in mind the likely effects of such a working will attract attention from the Wyld Hunt, probably prompted by Sidereals who detect a Solar-circle working preparing to warp reality on a Directional scale. The longer such efforts take, the more likely they'll be interrupted and things go boom. It isn't impossible: I mean, they did reject Creation's fate and replace it with one of their own design on a sacred continent. But I wager they are nowhere near common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:24:12-07:00","id":1129951,"title":"","content":"I think that it would be a location based effect (changing the metaphysics of a specific location) which would allow Celestial Sorcerers to treat Solar Circle Spells as Celestial Circle Spells for the purpose of learning and casting them (which would be a good Ambition 2 Solar Working). As long as Raksi is in her fortress of doom, she can learn and cast Solar Circle Spells as Celestial Circle Spells (but she is incapable of casting them when she is outside of her fortress of doom). It would explain why Raksi is reluctant to leave her base of operations, as she would lose access to her Solar Circle Spells when she is outside of its metaphysical borders. I would not suggest allowing them same for Solar Workings, as it would be odd to allow an Ambition 2 Solar Working to make Ambition 3 Solar Workings easier.<br /> <br /> On a slightly related note, could a Terrestrial Exalted Sorcerer use an Ambition 2 Solar Working to allow them to learn and use Celestial Circle Spells while they are within their base of operations? It would justify the classic hermit wizard archetype, as the Terrestrial Exalted Sorcerer would be much more powerful in their base of operations that outside of it. You could then end up with hundreds of small areas, probably centered around powerful manses, whose metaphysics allowed practitioners with Terrestrial Circle Sorcery to learn and use Celestial Circle Spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:37:34-07:00","id":1129958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1129943#post1129943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, hmmm.... If a maxxed out Celestial Circle Sorcerer can pull off the highest rank of Workings in as little as two years.... I think that Raksi should probably be assumed to have some method of casting Solar Circle spells by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a reason to make this assumption. If you assume that she may have, at one point or another in the past, used her sorcerous might to cast great one-off feats of magic which were terrifying in their scope, I could totally see that, though.<br /> <br /> I suspect if there's an obsession to do with anything, it would be with initiating into the Solar Circle, which is something distinct from just wanting to cast the spells, y'know? Spells are individually distinct 'things' but in-genre it's less about &quot;I want to learn Wyld-Shaping Technique&quot; and more like &quot;I want to gain power over the Wyld&quot; y'know what I mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:50:27-07:00","id":1129963,"title":"","content":"I'm not keen on letting workings give people spells (or charms) that they wouldn't normally be able to do. I think it'd be bad for the game.<br /> <br /> Plus, Raksi's obsessed with learning solar sorcery. If she can already cast Solar spells, then why is she so obsessed with learning to cast Solar spells?<br /> <br /> <i>Now I'm the queen of the swingers, the jungle V.I.P<br /> I reached the top and had to stop<br /> And that's what bothering me<br /> I want to be a Solar, Solar, and stroll right into town<br /> And be just like those other Solars<br /> I'm tired of monkeying around<br /> Now don't try to kid me, Solar, I'll make a deal with you<br /> What I desire is adamant power to make my dreams come true<br /> So give me the secret, Solar, clue me what to do<br /> Give me the power of adamant power so I can be like you<br /> <br /> Ooh-bitchdoo, I wan'na be like you<br /> I want to cast like you, summon like you, too<br /> You see it's true, an ape like me<br /> Can learn to be like you, too<br /> <br /> Can learn to be like me.</i><br /> <br /> (Then, you know, she eats your brain.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-16-2017, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T14:28:48-07:00","id":1129978,"title":"","content":"Hm, I wonder if Raksi would try to use a Solar Circle Working to attempt to fuse a Solar Exaltation to a Lunar Exaltation? She has not had access to any Solar Essences over the last 1,500 years, but she could capture a few Solar Exalted now and could probably convince a few Lunar Exalted to be test subjects. Do you think that it would be possible to fuse the two, to gain the best of both worlds, or would the recepient explode because of the overwhelming power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T15:03:30-07:00","id":1130004,"title":"","content":"I think that continuing in the 2e model wherein Exaltations are capturable widgets that can be poked and prodded runs fundamentally counter to the sense of myth and wonder that this edition is trying to emphasize in being Chosen. It is a *miracle*. It is synergeia, the divine partnering with the human. Even the most &quot;mechanical&quot; of the Exaltations, the Exigent, is difficult and dangerous to subvert. <br /> <br /> We have yet to get a nailed down 3e version of how Abyssals and Infernals were created, but I'm going to bet it wasn't by capturing glowing balls of light and then experimenting on them in a lab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":3907,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","user":"Aretii","date":". 08-16-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T16:24:00-07:00","id":1130029,"title":"","content":"I doubt it would be pseudo-physics experiments. I was thinking of a physical fusion of the Lunar to the body of the Solar, with the body of the Lunar consuming the body until only the necessary organs required to maintain Exaltation remain (perhaps functioning as a secondary brain and heart stored within the body of the Lunar). The personality of the Solar would necessarily be overwhelmed by the personality of the Lunar until the Solar and Lunar were effectively one personality and one body with two Exaltations. <br /> <br /> Of course, this would be a horrific fate for the Solar and likely unpleasant for the Lunar, but the Lunar could presumably survive it because of the faculty with shapeshifting. This is idle speculation, but I imagine that it is something that Raksi would decide to explore. I am thinking that it would be an Ambition 2 Solar Working. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:42:41-07:00","id":1130378,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that she'd suck out their po into a special occult container (as the exaltation is bonded to the Po) that includes their heart and brain, and then eat the whole thing, but that works too.<br /> Anyway, it should definitely involve sacrificing a Solar. Probably the Lunar's Solar mate (or maybe it'd be more effective with the Mate).<br /> <br /> As to the effects... well, in an individual game I might let it work if I thought it was interesting, but from a canon perspective, no it definitely won't work.<br /> <br /> It might do other things, like give the Lunar some other Solar-related bonus, though.<br /> <br /> And of course, whether it's effective or not, I'm sure Raksi would<i> try</i> it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:48:55-07:00","id":1130503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1129669#post1129669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, in the lead up to the release, Holden and Morke teased that a neat thing about the Caul was that the Lunars cut it away from the Loom of Fate. I'd buy THAT as being possible with an Ambition 3 Solar Working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends on whether the thing that they did qualifies as a subtle alteration of the cosmos.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf it's a more gross alteration, and thus subject to the spatial limits of even a working at that level, you'd need about 16,000 Ambition 3 Solar Workings to cover the whole island (assuming that a &quot;city-sized region&quot; covers about 25 square miles).<br /> <br /> \u200bI think the cause behind the Caul might be something else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:31:29-07:00","id":1130609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1129963#post1129963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not keen on letting workings give people spells (or charms) that they wouldn't normally be able to do. I think it'd be bad for the game.<br /> <br /> Plus, Raksi's obsessed with learning solar sorcery. If she can already cast Solar spells, then why is she so obsessed with learning to cast Solar spells?<br /> <br /> <i>Now I'm the queen of the swingers, the jungle V.I.P<br /> I reached the top and had to stop<br /> And that's what bothering me<br /> I want to be a Solar, Solar, and stroll right into town<br /> And be just like those other Solars<br /> I'm tired of monkeying around<br /> Now don't try to kid me, Solar, I'll make a deal with you<br /> What I desire is adamant power to make my dreams come true<br /> So give me the secret, Solar, clue me what to do<br /> Give me the power of adamant power so I can be like you<br /> <br /> Ooh-bitchdoo, I wan'na be like you<br /> I want to cast like you, summon like you, too<br /> You see it's true, an ape like me<br /> Can learn to be like you, too<br /> <br /> Can learn to be like me.</i><br /> <br /> (Then, you know, she eats your brain.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that, IF Raksi was still Obsessed in 3e about reaching the Solar Circle and IF a Solar ambition 3 Working could offer her a way to &quot;cheat&quot; her way into the Solar Circle, she's had more than enough time to enact said Working. But, as said Working would be unlikely to be flawless, I figured I'd ask everyone to speculate on the nature of the Cheat she used and what side effects it might have. Alternately you could speculate on what she's doing now.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you can't rewrite the rules of Sorcery even with a Solar 3 Working, then that's a moot point, but it's a legit question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:58:18-07:00","id":1130626,"title":"","content":"It occurred to me earlier this week that I've never read anything about whom exactly it was that Raksi had a solar bond with. That got me wondering if someone could initiate into Solar Circle sorcery while under the effect of that Wonder Twins-esque apocryphal charm in <i>Miracles of the Chosen</i>... or if the result would be an earth-shattering kaboom and somewhere across Creation a new Solar and Lunar exalting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1129943#post1129943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, hmmm.... If a maxxed out Celestial Circle Sorcerer can pull off the highest rank of Workings in as little as two years.... I think that Raksi should probably be assumed to have some method of casting Solar Circle spells by now. Assuming she's still obsessed about that anyway. Said method should also have some side effects however, as she likely had to cut a few corners here and there.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on how she might have done it or what the side effects are?</div> </div> </div> </div>If such a thing were possible at all, I'm thinking human sacrifice on a massive scale and pacts with third circle demons or one of the yozi themselves might be involved. Or maybe I'm still in the headspace reading <i>Elric: The Ruby Throne</i> last night put me into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T08:12:47-07:00","id":1130825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1130626#post1130626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe I'm still in the headspace reading <i>Elric: The Ruby Throne</i> last night put me into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she does live somewhat close to the Dreaming Sea...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T19:35:43-07:00","id":1131573,"title":"","content":"Just because a group of people is mechanically capable of pulling off Workings at the Solar level, doesn't mean we should expect it from them quite so routinely as the OP suggests. <br /> <br /> Let's not forget that the act of putting a Working together causes something of a &quot;disturbance in the Force,&quot; as it were - a Lunar wanting to attempt such a Working has a very real chance of attracting a band of unlikely heroes who want to put swords through her before her evil plan can come to fruition.<br /> <br /> (I also feel that <i>any</i> degree of sorcerous working is something of a big project, considering how it can take weeks of work at even the lowest levels and eat up significant amounts of resources; unless one is just about certain of its chances of success, one should probably consider very seriously whether to even do it at all.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T23:17:30-07:00","id":1131636,"title":"","content":"I think playing with exaltations should be beyond a sorcerous working. <br /> Or at the very least, it should be the <i>first step</i> and not the most difficult one. (yes, having flashbacks to the arguments about how quickly Twilights in 2E could set up their official mass production Alchemical line). <br /> <br /> That being said, an ambition 3 celestial working could create a second circle demon or notable god in power level. IT, something that could probably be a powerful opponent for an entire brotherhood of DB's or have other unique powers that might be quite impressive. An ambition 3 <i>solar</i> working can <i>Create a supernatural being of a singular nature and considerable<br /> power. </i>That says to me, at the very least an entity of Third Circle might and possibly something that might give any non-incarna a tussle. <br /> <br /> But I think people are missing the true power of the Lunar exalted-- <i>celestial</i> workings. They're safe(r), and faster than solar level workings, and they shouldn't be sneezed at. Ambition 3 Finesse 5 celestial workings are <i>well</i> within the reach of an experienced Lunar sorcerer, and they can do things like &quot;create a 2nd circle equivelent that haunts a city and kills any immaculate who tries to found a temple&quot; or spread mutatoins through the local ecosystem to turn the former realm satrapy into a deathworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:26:43-07:00","id":1131694,"title":"","content":"Informal Opinion Poll:<br /> <br /> Given how Lunar Exalted may have worse faculty for crafting than crafting-focused Terrestrial Exalted, and a larger bent than anyone else towards working with no tools, lots of disposable tools, or a vanishingly rare number of indispensable tools, and given their generally witchy, shaman-y theme...<br /> <br /> Do you think that more Lunar Exalted at least dip into Terrestrial Circle Sorcery than the Exalted of other Hosts?<br /> <br /> <br /> Spells are tools that the Lunar Exalted don't need to carry or worry about being stolen. Sorcerous workings are creations that don't require the same kind of investments and infrastructural resources as crafting, and if those workings are enchantments upon living creatures (or themselves) then they still don't have to worry about carrying or losing them. Plus, from a meta-standpoint, the XP is refunded if the working is gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even the Sidereal Exalted, who have such a limited Charmset to push them towards sorcery, have their large focus on the competitive investment sinkhole of Martial Arts. Even with all of them favoring all Martial Arts Abilities and Charms. Meanwhile, a number of Lunars could rely so heavily on inhuman forms that they never see a reason to learn a single Martial Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-20-2017, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:30:49-07:00","id":1131697,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded sorcerers are always going to outnumber every other Exalt types' sorcerers, even put together.<br /> <br /> (I <i>do</i> see more Lunars picking it up than Sidereals, though, simply by dint of there being about four times as many of them. However, I'd also think that a higher <i>percentage</i> of the Fivescore Fellowship learn sorcery than of the Lunar Exalted, born out of the combination of the necessities of their job, the longer lifespan of Sidereals, and Heaven seeming like a pretty good place to pick up sorcery from one source or another.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-20-2017, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:33:17-07:00","id":1131699,"title":"","content":"Proportionate to the size of their Host, I would agree with your reasoning that there are probably more Lunar sorcerers than anyone except Infernal Exalted, assuming that the Infernal relationship to sorcery remains broadly similar to 2E's.<br /> In absolute terms, obviously ten thousand dragons rule the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:46:18-07:00","id":1131708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1131697#post1131697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded sorcerers are always going to outnumber every other Exalt types' sorcerers, even put together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but as Aretii suggests, I was referring to proportion rather than actual numbers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I'd also think that a higher <i>percentage</i> of the Fivescore Fellowship learn sorcery than of the Lunar Exalted, born out of the combination of the necessities of their job, the longer lifespan of Sidereals, and Heaven seeming like a pretty good place to pick up sorcery from one source or another.) </div> </div> </div>For the Lunar Exalted, picking up sorcery could be driven by the necessity of <i>survival</i>, and the older Lunars who tattoo them could also initiate them into sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:48:55-07:00","id":1131710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1131708#post1131708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Lunar Exalted, picking up sorcery could be driven by the necessity of <i>survival</i>\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>In what scenario is a Lunar, one of the most dedicated &quot;survival&quot; splats in the game, finding himself that he is going to <i>die</i> if he doesn't learn sorcery?<br /> <br /> (Also, let's not forget, probably more than a few Exalts just aren't going to have it in them to learn sorcery, regardless of splat. You don't learn sorcery casually because it's useful, like learning how to shout for help in twenty languages; you learn it because you had something of that ineffable qualify in you, allowing you to undergo a transformation, from what you were, to a sorcerer. A Lunar elder can probably sniff out that potential - perhaps even literally - but they still can't teach sorcery to someone who lacks the capacity to learn it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-20-2017, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:54:12-07:00","id":1131757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1131697#post1131697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded sorcerers are always going to outnumber every other Exalt types' sorcerers, even put together.<br /> <br /> (I <i>do</i> see more Lunars picking it up than Sidereals, though, simply by dint of there being about four times as many of them. However, I'd also think that a higher <i>percentage</i> of the Fivescore Fellowship learn sorcery than of the Lunar Exalted, born out of the combination of the necessities of their job, the longer lifespan of Sidereals, and Heaven seeming like a pretty good place to pick up sorcery from one source or another.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with this. I think it's a bit easier for Sidereals to teach each other, as they all hang out together at their offices rather than being spread all over Creation.<br /> Not that it's massively easier, just a bit.<br /> I think also sorcery might be more useful for Sidereals at covering gaps in their abilities (with a small &quot;a&quot;) than for Lunars.<br /> <br /> I don't really see that Lunars are more likely to pick up sorcery than their native charms, for the sake of survival.<br /> I mean, learning sorcery isn't a question just of having it or not. It's a matter of learning it rather than learning something else. If a Lunar is, say, leading his tribe in a battle for existence against a Realm legion, I'd think he'd be just as likely to learn some Charisma or Stamina charms than sorcery.<br /> <br /> Either way though, I doubt there's a massive difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think a lower percentage of Dragonblood probably learn it though, as most DBs either have less access to a teacher than Lunars/Sidereals do, and in the Realm there's a certain social pressure against learning it.<br /> All of them have generally more access to teachers than Solars though (on average).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-20-2017, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:43:30-07:00","id":1131808,"title":"","content":"I don't think Lunars would generally need to consider sorcery in terms of survival, but it seems like something that would be significant in the possibilities of how they can confound their enemies in a variety of ways. I can see a Lunar of the Silver Pact going to sorcery for the sake of having even more methods of attacking the Realm with more flexibility than can be effectively adapted to.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut that doesn't change my perspective on how many Lunars use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T15:32:38-07:00","id":1131910,"title":"","content":"The pagan shamanistic bent of some of the splat's themes makes me think there might be a higher proportion of dabblers than among the Dragonlords, but without an organized system to teach it like the Heptagram (or perhaps much in the way of organization at all), I don't see more of them making it their principal focus. Your Raksis are probably at least as rare as your Mnemons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T01:31:18-07:00","id":1132117,"title":"","content":"Ah, so lots of Lunars with just 1 or spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T18:17:02-07:00","id":1132880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1129772#post1129772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, removing a continent from the Loom (very useful when battling Sidereals) is pretty damn significant.<br /> <br /> Other ideas:<br /> Creating a huge magical oasis teeming with life in the middle of the desert, protected by massive enchanted walls that make it invisible, to create a hidden kingdom for the Lunar's subjects, from which they can strike at the Realm.<br /> Create a flying island full of monsters that can be used as a mobile battlestation.<br /> Create a huge Wyld zone all the way around a country, stopping the Realm daring to attack it.<br /> Enchant a land so that those who eat its food while pregnant give birth to beastmen of the Lunar's totem (what, you think Lunar's give birth to all those beastmen by themselves?)<br /> Create an army of golems inhabited by the souls of the dead of the Lunar's tribe.<br /> Curse a Satrapy so that all children born there are hideous mutants.<br /> Curse a Satrapy so that it becomes a massive wyld zone.<br /> Bless (or curse) the Lunar's subjects so that when they die, their souls possess large animals (lions, horses, elephants, etc).<br /> Bless (or curse) the Lunar's subjects so that when they die, they transform into elementals of the local elements.<br /> Change time at the summit of a mountain so that students who go there can do awesome training montages under the Lunar's tutelage, and become (still mortal) kung-fu masters in a few days.<br /> Create a massive fortress which can think for itself, shoot ballista, use statues to defend itself, and move walls to confuse attackers (you don't live there, you just make the Realm think you do so they waste time trying to invade it).<br /> Bless the entire country's land so that one farmer can produce enough food for 100 people, allowing the people to move into other jobs and spark a massive economic boom.<br /> Create rings of stone that, when someone walks into them, lets them travel along a mysterious fog-shrouded, eerie path, leading to another stone circle, allowing someone to cross a kingdom in an hour. Multiple rings allow the inhabitants to travel all over the country, allowing troops and trade to move wherever they're needed incredibly quickly.<br /> Create a horde of terrifying flying monsters for your armies to ride.<br /> Turn thousands of people into were-wolves (or were-horses, or were-owls, or whatever).<br /> Enchant a land with a strange fog that drives the Lunar's enemies mad, but leaves her subjects and friends untouched.<br /> Mess with dragon lines, so that Satrapy's manses stop working (or blow up), while creating new demesnes far away in the wilderness.<br /> Create a radiation-breathing, super-strong, super-tough, super-stealthy, amphibious Kaiju, who really hates Immaculate temples, and who who lurks in the Inner Sea and periodically appears to destroy cities with Immaculate temples in.<br /> <br /> I think the main thing PCs are going to encounter, in terms of Solar workings made by Lunars, is magically enchanted forests/mountains/countries, or giant ravenous monsters created to attack the Realm (or whoever).<br /> And things to hide them from Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, can i use these examples in a thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T06:23:36-07:00","id":1132990,"title":"","content":"Go for it. Which thread?<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually don't think all those examples are that interesting, some are a bit repetitive, so I'd like to see if others take inspiration from them to come up with weirder and more interesting ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T08:55:02-07:00","id":1133030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1132990#post1132990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go for it. Which thread?<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually don't think all those examples are that interesting, some are a bit repetitive, so I'd like to see if others take inspiration from them to come up with weirder and more interesting ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1133029-sorcerous-workings-got-any-ideas\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1133029-sorcerous-workings-got-any-ideas\"> Sorcerous workings - got any ideas? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1133029-sorcerous-workings-got-any-ideas\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1133029-sorcerous-workings-got-any-ideas </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I've never been good at imagining things for sorcerous workings, thus, this thread. Please note what circle, it should be. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I always had problems with visualising sorcerous workings. So a something like this is really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T03:05:09-07:00","id":1134094,"title":"","content":"I think that it's a mistake to go from &quot;the rules technically allow this&quot; to &quot;everyone does this.&quot;<br /> <br /> My feeling is that especially at the high end, the rules tend to be generous to PCs. My default assumption is that there has been maybe a dozen Ambition 3 Solar workings done ever. I don't mean ones done by Lunars, I mean ones done by <i>anyone</i>, including Solars. Maybe one or two of those has been since the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> It just isn't something that you can really allow to happen more than a few times in history without the setting getting really, really weird (or unless you start to contort yourself into knots to explain why all these reality-shifts went unnoticed by almost everyone, or scaling down Ambition 3 workings to the point where they're no longer as impressive.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1129669#post1129669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Them's some broad assumptions on the number of Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> That said, in the lead up to the release, Holden and Morke teased that a neat thing about the Caul was that the Lunars cut it away from the Loom of Fate. I'd buy THAT as being possible with an Ambition 3 Solar Working.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Caul was &quot;just&quot; Ambition 2, since you're just altering one major metaphysical property of a region. Ambition 3 would be if you were moving it outside of time and space or to another dimension entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T03:15:53-07:00","id":1134097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1134094#post1134094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> why all these reality-shifts went unnoticed by almost everyone</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe fact that they're limited to being subtle alterations would seem to be a great help in being difficult to notice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquiliion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Caul was &quot;just&quot; Ambition 2, since you're just altering one major metaphysical property of a region.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOf a <b>city-sized</b> region. City-sized.<br /> <br /> \u200bI believe that somebody in this thread has made a rough calculation of how many city-sizes the Caul consists of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T06:38:43-07:00","id":1134127,"title":"","content":"The thread about how beastmen are made, made me think that turning loads of people into beastmen of some kind, is probably a suitable Lunar working. Or making all babies born beastmen, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T06:52:54-07:00","id":1134130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1134127#post1134127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thread about how beastmen are made, made me think that turning loads of people into beastmen of some kind, is probably a suitable Lunar working. Or making all babies born beastmen, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also possible is the idea of Lunars pulling off a <i>Nine Princes in Amber</i> and finding or cultivating a place in the Wyld where they can march off an entire generation of beastmen to fight for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-26-2017, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T07:11:22-07:00","id":1134132,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I could see that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T07:18:51-07:00","id":1134135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1134094#post1134094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it's a mistake to go from &amp;quot;the rules technically allow this&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;everyone does this.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> My feeling is that especially at the high end, the rules tend to be generous to PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. We already make this separation for things like XP curves, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T07:24:47-07:00","id":1134138,"title":"","content":"Rather than world-redefining Solar-level workings which almost never happen, and never will happen again except when the plot demands it, I'm much more interested in the kinds of sorcerous working that Lunars perform <i>frequently</i>.<br /> <br /> Things like turning their followers into beastmen or werecreatures, certainly. But also modifications to themselves, and making various enchanted tools which aren't as expensive or durable as artifacts, and therefore are more disposable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T08:40:25-07:00","id":1134150,"title":"","content":"Well, a Lunar sorcerer in my Dreaming Sea game bought a slave who had been blind from birth, in the hopes that she would provide him an extra Means for his Working. (Essentially an invisibility cloak; by only having sightless people work on it, that would better catalyze the magic. Even the sorcerer wouldn't enter the chamber where it was being made without blindfolding himself first and only working at night.)<br /> <br /> Per his directions, she forged a spear, killed an animal raised in the dark with it, and sewed its skin into a cloak; but the plan went somewhat awry when she escaped into the desert with an ifrit and Exalted as a Twilight without completing the project. The Lunar sent a demon to go collect her (not knowing she had taken the Second Breath), but he's hedging his bets; if it doesn't come back with her soon, he'll just buy another slave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T11:00:04-07:00","id":1134187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1134138#post1134138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than world-redefining Solar-level workings which almost never happen, and never will happen again except when the plot demands it, I'm much more interested in the kinds of sorcerous working that Lunars perform <i>frequently</i>.<br /> <br /> Things like turning their followers into beastmen or werecreatures, certainly. But also modifications to themselves, and making various enchanted tools which aren't as expensive or durable as artifacts, and therefore are more disposable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine they devote a <i>lot</i> of workings to secrecy, security, protection, and various sorts of defenses, just based on their current situation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T11:22:29-07:00","id":1134194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1134187#post1134187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine they devote a <i>lot</i> of workings to secrecy, security, protection, and various sorts of defenses, just based on their current situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And whatever workings would allow them to find and retrieve new Lunar Exalts before the Wyld Hunt or Sidereals find them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T16:33:16-07:00","id":1134296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1134194#post1134194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And whatever workings would allow them to find and retrieve new Lunar Exalts before the Wyld Hunt or Sidereals find them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather that be something innate to Lunars (eg. like my idea for Lunar Exaltation being akin to a &quot;call&quot;, with an older Lunar receiving a visitation from Luna telling them to become your mentor - this would explain the Lunar mentor / student relationships, which have always been a major part of the splat, in a more concrete way.)<br /> <br /> That has the advantage of making Lunars a bit more unique, and it also explains why Lunars are able to find each other when both Sidereals and DBs have just as much incentive to hunt new Lunars and far more resources to devote to it.<br /> <br /> Granted that you can just say &quot;the Sidereals and DBs <i>do</i> find most new Lunars, and they just reincarnate until they get lucky and are found by a Lunar&quot;, but that's a bit unsatisfying. Especially given that Sworn Brotherhoods are apparently being made into an innate DB thing, I think it would make sense to give Lunars some sort of innate feature tying them together and giving them an edge at finding newly-Exalted Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-09-2018, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T19:13:29-07:00","id":1134322,"title":"","content":"It does seem appropriate, being exemplary hunters is very much a Lunar sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T07:31:25-07:00","id":1134458,"title":"","content":"It doesn't sound too out there for an Essence 4-5 Perception Charm, maybe one that works based on the user's Caste and the current phase of the moon (since a fresh Exalt will obviously be untattooed and their Caste will match the phase).<br /> <br /> Though to be fair, Lunars don't necessarily need to find a newbie right away; they have an advantage in moving quickly from place to place over your average Wyld Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T07:34:58-07:00","id":1134463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129472-using-lunar-sorcery?p=1134296#post1134296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather that be something innate to Lunars (eg. like my idea for Lunar Exaltation being akin to a &quot;call&quot;, with an older Lunar receiving a visitation from Luna telling them to become your mentor - this would explain the Lunar mentor / student relationships, which have always been a major part of the splat, in a more concrete way.)<br /> <br /> That has the advantage of making Lunars a bit more unique, and it also explains why Lunars are able to find each other when both Sidereals and DBs have just as much incentive to hunt new Lunars and far more resources to devote to it.<br /> <br /> Granted that you can just say &quot;they <i>do</i> find most new Lunars, and they just reincarnate until they get lucky and are found by a Lunar&quot;, but that's a bit unsatisfying. Especially given that Sworn Brotherhoods are apparently being made into an innate DB thing, I think it would make sense to give Lunars some sort of innate feature tying them together and giving them an edge at finding newly-Exalted Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea better.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted ARE the only Host whose every member is visited personally by Luna at the moment of their Second Breath. Given that is one of the few things that sets them apart from the Solar Exalted, it only makes sense to expand upon it.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of Luna visiting Lunars again later in life to tell them about the rebirth of a new brother or sister.<br /> <br /> I love the idea that the Lunar she visits may not even WANT to go to the trouble of hunting down a student, let alone teaching them. Or who would track them down and spirit them away, but refuse to teach them. Or someone who refuses to search for them, but might agree to teach them out of guilt for not going out to rescue them.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of Luna's visit to a willing Lunar sparking a HUNT. This was actually suggested as a major adventure (a &quot;savage adventure&quot;, if you will) back in the First Edition Lunar manual, but it was bogged down by all of the terrible &quot;faux barbarian&quot; bits, and then rather neglected in Second Edition's rather sterilized approach to Lunar Exaltation.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of Luna and her Chosen having this loose but intimate web of interconnections; bonds, mentor/student relations, debts, favors, oaths. A Silver Pact, if you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T08:16:53-07:00","id":1134472,"title":"","content":"They certainly need something to explain how they're so good at finding new Lunars and getting them to safety compared to Sidereals, who apparently can detect new Celestial Exaltations on the Loom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}